Based on the search results, I found relevant information about the verification request callback handler in the matrix-rust-sdk.

The `VerificationRequestListener` is a trait that serves as a listener passed over the FFI to report changes to a verification request, with a callback that should be called on the Rust side.(no content)The `set_changes_listener` method can be used to set a listener for changes in the verification request, and the given callback will be called whenever the state changes. The method signature shows:

```rust
pub fn set_changes_listener(&self, listener: Box<dyn VerificationRequestListener>) {
    let stream = self.inner.changes();
    self.runtime.spawn(Self::changes_listener(self.inner.to_owned(), stream, listener));
}
```

Additionally, a verification flow usually starts as a `VerificationRequest`, which can be accepted or needs to be accepted by the other side, and once both sides have agreed to perform verification, the request can transition into one of the supported verification flows like `SasVerification` or `QrVerification`.

For more detailed documentation on the verification APIs, you can visit the official docs at https://docs.rs/matrix-sdk/ or the GitHub repository at https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-rust-sdk.


